meta {
  name: Get Assessment Start Info
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/assessments/slots/{{assessmentSlotId}}/start?application_course_id={{applicationCourseId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  application_course_id: {{applicationCourseId}}
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Assessment Room screen: returns the slot's timing window, the template's
  section breakdown, its instructions (heading + description + an
  optional client-defined icon key), `total_marks`, and
  `total_duration_secs` — both computed as sums over the currently-approved
  normal paper's questions (marks summed for `total_marks`,
  time_limit_secs summed for `total_duration_secs`; both 0 if no normal
  paper is approved yet) — neither is an admin-declared template field
  anymore. `has_active_trial_paper` tells the client whether to
  show/enable "Take Trial of Assessment". `is_within_window` tells the
  frontend whether the slot can be started right now; `has_window_passed`
  distinguishes "too early" from "missed it".

  `application_course_id` is optional — pass it to get `my_attempt`
  (`{id, status}` or `null`) so the Room screen can render "Resume
  Assessment" instead of "Start Assessment" for a returning student.
}
